58,58,58.json,58_L1,Confounding factors and unknowns affecting token probabilities,2,Experiments,0.136804,"In Section 3.1 we choose to use perplexity on base models as our measure because it can be easily applied on the sentence level regardless of how the sentence is tokenized, and also correlates directly with token generation probabilities (e.g., sentence x has lower perplexity than y generally implies that sentence x is more likely to be generated than y)."
